{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Arithmetic.PrimitiveSetsAbove\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Arithmetic.LPrimitive\n\nPrimitive-set-only L-multiple skeleton extracted from Lichtman's proof of the\nErdos primitive set conjecture.\n\nThe paper defines\n\n`L_a = { b * a : every prime p | b satisfies p >= P(a) }`,\n\nwhere `P(a)` is the largest prime factor of `a`, and calls a set `L`-primitive\nwhen no distinct member is an `L`-multiple of another.\n\nThis file installs the finite/order-theoretic skeleton only.  The analytic\nparts of Lichtman's proof, such as log-density of `L_A`, Mertens estimates,\nodd-prime strength, and the special `p = 2` bound, remain explicit witness\nsurfaces.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Arithmetic\n\n/-- All prime factors of `m` are at least `B`. -/\ndef PrimeFactorsGE (m B : ℕ) : Prop :=\n  ∀ ⦃p : ℕ⦄, Nat.Prime p → p ∣ m → B ≤ p\n\n/-- `P` is a largest prime factor of `a`. -/\ndef IsLargestPrimeFactorOf (P a : ℕ) : Prop :=\n  Nat.Prime P ∧ P ∣ a ∧ ∀ ⦃q : ℕ⦄, Nat.Prime q → q ∣ a → q ≤ P\n\n/--\n`n` is an `L`-multiple of `a`, witnessed using a largest prime factor `P` of `a`.\n\nThis is the direct Lean surface for\n\n`n ∈ L_a` iff `n = b * a` and every prime divisor of `b` is at least `P(a)`.\n-/\ndef LMultiple (a n : ℕ) : Prop :=\n  ∃ P : ℕ, IsLargestPrimeFactorOf P a ∧ ∃ b : ℕ, n = b * a ∧ PrimeFactorsGE b P\n\n/-- Set of `L`-multiples of `a`. -/\ndef LMultiplesOf (a : ℕ) : Set ℕ :=\n  {n | LMultiple a n}\n\n/-- Set of `L`-multiples generated by a set `A`. -/\ndef LMultiplesOfSet (A : Set ℕ) : Set ℕ :=\n  {n | ∃ a ∈ A, LMultiple a n}\n\n/-- `A` is `L`-primitive when no distinct member is an `L`-multiple of another. -/\ndef LPrimitiveSet (A : Set ℕ) : Prop :=\n  ∀ ⦃a a' : ℕ⦄, a ∈ A → a' ∈ A → LMultiple a a' → a = a'\n\n/-- Finite `L`-primitive specialization. -/\ndef LPrimitiveFinset (A : Finset ℕ) : Prop :=\n  LPrimitiveSet (A : Set ℕ)\n\n/-- An `L`-multiple is an ordinary multiple. -/\ntheorem LMultiple.dvd {a n : ℕ} (h : LMultiple a n) : a ∣ n := by\n  rcases h with ⟨_P, _hP, b, rfl, _hb⟩\n  exact ⟨b, by rw [Nat.mul_comm]⟩\n\n/-- If `P` is a largest prime factor of `a`, then `a ∈ L_a`. -/\ntheorem LMultiple.self_of_largestPrimeFactor {a P : ℕ}\n    (hP : IsLargestPrimeFactorOf P a) :\n    LMultiple a a := by\n  refine ⟨P, hP, 1, ?_, ?_⟩\n  · simp\n  · intro p hp hpdvd\n    exact (Nat.Prime.not_dvd_one hp hpdvd).elim\n\n/-- Ordinary primitive sets are `L`-primitive. -/\ntheorem PrimitiveSet.toLPrimitiveSet {A : Set ℕ}\n    (hA : PrimitiveSet A) :\n    LPrimitiveSet A := by\n  intro a a' ha ha' hL\n  exact hA ha ha' hL.dvd\n\n/-- Finite ordinary primitive sets are finite `L`-primitive sets. -/\ntheorem PrimitiveFinset.toLPrimitiveFinset {A : Finset ℕ}\n    (hA : PrimitiveFinset A) :\n    LPrimitiveFinset A :=\n  PrimitiveSet.toLPrimitiveSet hA\n\n/-- Membership in `LMultiplesOfSet` is union membership over generators. -/\ntheorem mem_LMultiplesOfSet_iff {A : Set ℕ} {n : ℕ} :\n    n ∈ LMultiplesOfSet A ↔ ∃ a ∈ A, n ∈ LMultiplesOf a := by\n  rfl\n\n/--\nLichtman trichotomy input.\n\nThe paper proves that if `L_a` and `L_a'` meet, then one generator is an\n`L`-multiple of the other.  We keep this as an explicit finite combinatorial\ninput until the largest-prime-factor arithmetic proof is fully formalized.\n-/\nstructure LTrichotomyInput where\n  trichotomy :\n    ∀ ⦃a a' x : ℕ⦄,\n      1 < a →\n      1 < a' →\n      LMultiple a x →\n      LMultiple a' x →\n        LMultiple a a' ∨ LMultiple a' a\n\nnamespace LTrichotomyInput\n\n/--\nFor an `L`-primitive set, distinct generators have disjoint `L`-multiple\nsurfaces, assuming the Lichtman trichotomy input.\n-/\ntheorem not_common_LMultiple_of_lprimitive\n    (T : LTrichotomyInput)\n    {A : Set ℕ}\n    (hA : LPrimitiveSet A)\n    {a a' x : ℕ}\n    (ha : a ∈ A)\n    (ha' : a' ∈ A)\n    (haa' : a ≠ a')\n    (ha_gt : 1 < a)\n    (ha'_gt : 1 < a')\n    (hx : LMultiple a x)\n    (hx' : LMultiple a' x) :\n    False := by\n  rcases T.trichotomy ha_gt ha'_gt hx hx' with h | h\n  · exact haa' (hA ha ha' h)\n  · exact haa' ((hA ha' ha h).symm)\n\nend LTrichotomyInput\n\n/-- Density data for a single `L_a` surface. -/\nstructure LMultipleDensityWitness (a : ℕ) where\n  density : ℝ\n  density_law : Prop\n  density_law_holds : density_law\n\n/-- Log-density data for `L_A`. -/\nstructure LPrimitiveLogDensityWitness (A : Set ℕ) where\n  logDensity : ℝ\n  densitySum : ℝ\n  density_eq_sum : logDensity = densitySum\n\n/--\nAnalytic input corresponding to the Lichtman local `L`-primitive bound.\n\nThis is intentionally a witness packet: it names the density/Mertens/local\nestimate obligations without pretending they are proved by this skeleton.\n-/\nstructure LichtmanLocalBoundInput where\n  localBoundLaw : Prop\n  localBoundLaw_holds : localBoundLaw\n  lDensityLaw : Prop\n  lDensityLaw_holds : lDensityLaw\n  mertensProductLaw : Prop\n  mertensProductLaw_holds : mertensProductLaw\n\nend InfoGeometry.Arithmetic\n","mtime":1778076470227}